<mddoc>
	<docpage target="README.md">
		<section title="Dot Notation Parser">
			<badge-poser type="version"/>
			<badge-poser type="downloads"/>
			<badge-poser type="license"/>
			<badge-github-action name="QuorumCollection/DotNotationParser" workflow-file="ci.yml"/>
			<badge-coveralls name="github/QuorumCollection/DotNotationParser"/>
			<text><![CDATA[
DotNotationParser turns dot-delimited paths into an ordered list of keys. Use it when configuration, request parameters, or nested data need a compact path syntax. For example, `account.profile.name` becomes `[ 'account', 'profile', 'name' ]`.

Keys may contain dots when wrapped in double quotes. Escape a literal double quote with a backslash. The parser reports invalid paths with the character offset that caused the error, so callers can return useful feedback.

]]></text>
			<section title="Requirements">
				<composer-requires/>
			</section>
			<section title="Installing">
				<composer-install/>
			</section>
			<section title="Example">
				<source name="example/example.php" lang="php"/>
				<exec cmd="php example/example.php"  format="code-block"/>
			</section>
			<section title="Documentation">
				<file name="src/DotNotationParser.php"/>
			</section>
		</section>
	</docpage>
</mddoc>
